  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two machines",
      "items": [
        "core owns the role machine and is Qt-free; PetStroll owns the walk, PetStage the scene, PetHide the hide",
        "Every drawn state maps to code: Role::Idle, Thinking, Study, Celebrate, ClickReact, Pickup, Ask and Sleep; PetStroll Phase::Waiting/Walking; PetHide; PetStage",
        "QML reads only the PetPose value — action, scene, review sign — never a state enum",
        "Priority: Idle < Situational < Event < Click < Drag; Study, Ask and Sleep are held states the pet returns to",
        "Three clicks in two seconds turn the click pose Angry",
        "A self-ended nap or a wake from the budget's sleep stretches once before idling (ADR 0098)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Wander, hide and trip · ADR 0076 + 0155",
      "items": [
        "120-300 s of true idle before a stroll; the gait comes from the pet's data (glide, float, hop, trot, pounce)",
        "A stroll walks up to two steps with pauses between; a pounce gait still takes exactly one",
        "A step ending at the work-area edge rolls 70% into a hide",
        "Nothing times a hide out: a drag out past 0.8 of the width or a click on the sliver ends it (ADR 0095)",
        "At 0.5% the stroll becomes a taskbar trip instead, and the role clock holds while it runs (ADR 0155)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Rolls and signs · ADR 0123 + 0125",
      "items": [
        "PetStage owns the scene lottery, the entry timeline and the frames; the controller only publishes (ADR 0123)",
        "The 1/6 scene and 1/12 yawn rolls live in the role machine's idle turn",
        "Review answers branch: remembered Celebrate, forgotten Encourage, ignored Angry",
        "Each pet draws its own review sign (ADR 0125); the behavior block tunes the idle odds (ADR 0094)"
      ]
    }
  ]
